WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.000
Try not to think of a white bear. A simple order begins a problem.

2
00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:14.000
In 1987 volunteers reported their thoughts and rang a bell when the bear appeared.

3
00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:21.000
The bell could count reports. It could not read the mind.

4
00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:28.000
Later analysis found rebound after suppression more consistently than an immediate increase.

5
00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:34.000
The lesson isn't that meditation fails. It's that forcing silence and guiding attention are different.

6
00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:40.000
Evidence before promise. A recorded preference is not a proven brainwave change.
